\name{cellucid_layout_section_open}
\alias{cellucid_layout_section_open}
\title{Open or close a section}
\usage{
cellucid_layout_section_open(viewer, section, open)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{section}{A sidebar section by its title (Visualization, Navigation, \ldots) or its id. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{open}{True opens it, false closes it. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Open or close a section of the sidebar (docked or floating).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{layout.section.open} (Layout). It changes the viewer's layout: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{layout}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_layout_section_open(viewer, open = FALSE,
      section = "Visualization")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
